From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 03:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] fat: write cluster and size little-endian

rom/filesys/fat converts these on read -- FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER() in fat_fs.h,
AROS_LE2LONG on file_size in lock.c -- and not on write. On a little-endian
host both are no-ops and the asymmetry is invisible. On a big-endian one the
field goes to disk in host order and comes back swapped, which is what makes
the card poison itself: a boot writes its font indexes, and every boot after
that hangs in OpenDiskFont.

Measured with bytes rather than argued. A boot wrote a 17-byte file and
copied C:Echo, 1944 bytes; on the host the sizes read back as 0x11000000 and
0x98070000 -- reversed 17 and 1944 -- while the file *contents* were
byte-identical to the originals. So the block path is clean, the SD backend
is innocent, and the loss is entirely in how the fields are composed. With
this applied: sizes 17 and 1944, and mcopy reads both files back.

**Write side only, and that boundary is measured, not stylistic.** The same
change with the read-side raw comparisons replaced by FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER()
-- in GetDirEntryByCluster and in Rename -- takes the boot from 3 of 6 runs
reaching the desktop to 0 of 6. Those comparisons never match on a
big-endian host, so GetParentDir's search silently always fails; making it
succeed wakes a code path that has not run here and does not work. The raw
comparison is accidentally load-bearing. Fixing it is its own problem, and
is recorded in AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0007.md.

The date fields are also left alone. They are symmetrically unconverted --
ConvertDOSDate produces a native UWORD and ConvertFATDate is handed the raw
field -- so AROS round-trips them among itself; they are wrong on disk for
anything else reading the card, which is a smaller and separate problem.
Converting them was measured too, and is not what broke the boot.

Upstream defect on every big-endian AROS target; m68k-amiga, ppc-native and
ppc-morphos share this code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c | 10 ++++++++--
 rom/filesys/fat/ops.c      | 18 ++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c b/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
index 7296ca9474..f1e1542301 100644
--- a/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
+++ b/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
@@ -578,8 +578,14 @@ void FillDirEntry(struct DirEntry *de, UBYTE attr, ULONG cluster,
     de->e.entry.create_time_tenth = ds.ds_Tick % (TICKS_PER_SECOND * 2)
         / (TICKS_PER_SECOND / 10);
 
-    de->e.entry.first_cluster_lo = cluster & 0xffff;
-    de->e.entry.first_cluster_hi = cluster >> 16;
+    /* Little-endian on the way out. Upstream converts these on read
+     * (FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER, lock.c) and not on write, which is a no-op on a
+     * little-endian host and a swapped field on a big-endian one.
+     * WRITE SIDE ONLY -- the read-side raw comparisons are deliberately left
+     * as upstream has them; substituting them as well is what a bisect
+     * identified as breaking the boot. See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0007.md. */
+    de->e.entry.first_cluster_lo = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster & 0xffff);
+    de->e.entry.first_cluster_hi = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster >> 16);
 
     de->e.entry.file_size = 0;
 }
diff --git a/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c b/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
index 979dca67fb..3d291c0c67 100644
--- a/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
+++ b/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
@@ -749,8 +749,8 @@ LONG OpCreateDir(struct ExtFileLock *dirlock, UBYTE *name, ULONG namelen,
     cluster = dh.ioh.first_cluster;
     if (cluster == dh.ioh.sb->rootdir_cluster)
         cluster = 0;
-    sde.e.entry.first_cluster_lo = cluster & 0xffff;
-    sde.e.entry.first_cluster_hi = cluster >> 16;
+    sde.e.entry.first_cluster_lo = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster & 0xffff);
+    sde.e.entry.first_cluster_hi = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster >> 16);
     UpdateDirEntry(&sde, glob);
 
     /* Clear all remaining entries (the first of which marks the end of the
@@ -886,9 +886,11 @@ LONG OpWrite(struct ExtFileLock *lock, UBYTE *data, ULONG want,
                 glob);
             GetDirEntry(&dh, lock->gl->dir_entry, &de, glob);
 
-            de.e.entry.file_size = lock->gl->size;
-            de.e.entry.first_cluster_lo = lock->gl->first_cluster & 0xffff;
-            de.e.entry.first_cluster_hi = lock->gl->first_cluster >> 16;
+            de.e.entry.file_size = AROS_LONG2LE(lock->gl->size);
+            de.e.entry.first_cluster_lo =
+                AROS_WORD2LE(lock->gl->first_cluster & 0xffff);
+            de.e.entry.first_cluster_hi =
+                AROS_WORD2LE(lock->gl->first_cluster >> 16);
 
             de.e.entry.attr |= ATTR_ARCHIVE;
             UpdateDirEntry(&de, glob);
@@ -1060,9 +1062,9 @@ LONG OpSetFileSize(struct ExtFileLock *lock, LONG offset, LONG whence,
     }
 
     /* Clusters are fixed, now update the directory entry */
-    de.e.entry.first_cluster_lo = first & 0xffff;
-    de.e.entry.first_cluster_hi = first >> 16;
-    de.e.entry.file_size = size;
+    de.e.entry.first_cluster_lo = AROS_WORD2LE(first & 0xffff);
+    de.e.entry.first_cluster_hi = AROS_WORD2LE(first >> 16);
+    de.e.entry.file_size = AROS_LONG2LE(size);
     de.e.entry.attr |= ATTR_ARCHIVE;
     UpdateDirEntry(&de, glob);
 
